KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ vector deduced from an iterator pair: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
`std::vector v(a.begin(), a.end())' uses vector's deduction guide from an
iterator pair ([vector.overview]: vector(InputIter, InputIter, Allocator =
Allocator()) -> vector<iter-value-type<InputIter>, Allocator>).  CBMC
undefined __cpp_deduction_guides when preprocessing, so libstdc++'s guides
were compiled out, deduced vector<iterator, iterator> by position, and
v.size() was not 3.  Also needed: a guide parameter with a default
argument ([over.match.viable]/2.3), and undeduced guide template
parameters taking their defaults, with substitution failures removing the
guide ([temp.deduct.general]/5, /8).
